nty decorative  ears of course the size and shape of  batman's ears have varied over the years  heck they're barely even visible on  applex suit but they're always there  and while they may not be quite as  iconic as the cape or even the insignia  batman's ears have become a staple of  the hero's design  and they've even gone on to influence a  handful of other super folk over the  years  including catwoman catman daredevil and  black panther  from the unmistakably snazzy effects of  the camping 1960 series to robert  pattinson just straight up laying into a  street thug in the batman  it's clear that bruce wayne has always  been a punchy kind of guy there are a  few good reasons why this has become  such a crucial part of the character  for one there's a basic primal thrill to  be found in it even though fighting  isn't all that fun in real life  fictional combat is exhilarating like  almost nothing else  why else do action movies even exist so  any writer who needs to inject a little  excitement into their batman story  simply needs to provide gotham's  guardian with a pace to punch a stomach  to kick or a limb to snap  and voila instant entertainment have you  ever danced with the devil in the pale  moonlight  [Music]  from batman's in story perspective  criminals might not find him so  intimidating if they knew they stood a  chance against him in a fist fight  so his reputation as a master of several  martial arts disciplines makes it easier  to intimidate potential foes  and also allows him to solve the  majority of his problems with a  well-placed knock to a skull or tent  some of batman's adversaries might be  too powerful to beat up of course  while others might be smart enough to  avoid a punching contest with him  but for your typical everyday purse  snatcher type a haymaker wrapped in a  back glove will always do the trick  and then some they don't call him the  world's greatest detective for nothing  you know  batman might be able to throw a punch  like 