stacle course complete with faux  opponents  similar to the early version of the  danger room in xavier's school for  gifted youngsters  the batcave also provides a natural  habitat for a colony of actual bats  because after all he is called batman  bruce wayne's list of allies is a long  one indeed it could include  any number of individuals formerly or  currently known as robin  multiple crime fighters currently are  formerly known as batgirl  catwoman a few members of the gotham  city police department lucius fox and a  handful of his immediate family members  and of course bruce wayne's longtime  butler alfred pennyworth  and if a mission requires a trip abroad  or off planet he has the rest of the  justice league to call upon for  assistance  even other versions of the character  tend to have friends for example terry  mcginnis primary running buddy in his  future version of gotham happens to be  bruce wayne himself  even the horrifying batman who laughs as  a bunch of creepy vampire type creatures  and robin outfits on  leashes and sure in theory batman works  alone  most likely so he can tell people that  he works alone which is all well and  good for sounding all brooding and  dangerous  but in practice batman usually works  with a big old heap of pals  to some extent this is true of every  major superhero but it's doubly  important for batman as without plenty  of personal connections to keep him  grounded he could end up walking a very  dark path indeed  gadgets are a must-have for any  superhero who doesn't have any actual  superpowers so it follows that batman  has plenty  heck he's even got that iconic utility  belt to carry them all around in  one man's tool is another man's weapon  in your mind perhaps  there aren't many things you can't turn  into enough the police weren't getting  it done  batman's full list of gizmos is pretty  much impossible to count but one thing  that is certain is that as far as  equipment is concerned  it's very rare for him 